WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.800
- That was a look at
their new Bravo series

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.260
SWV and Xscape the Queens of R &amp; B.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.050
So Kandi, could you tell us
what happens on this new show?

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:08.190
- Well

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.500
You know, we were just
really following the journey

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.800
of two strong female
groups of the nineties

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.940
and showing you you know,

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:16.230
the behind the scenes of what it takes

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.880
to make a show like this happens.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:19.410
So you get to follow that journey.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.420
You get to see what happened
in our personal lives.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.710
And then, you know,

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.695
obviously we are too strong female groups.

00:00:25.695 --> 00:00:26.528
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:26.528 --> 00:00:28.530
- So you can see how sometimes, you know

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:31.560
we do not, not necessarily
see eye to eye, but we

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.393
figure it out.

00:00:32.393 --> 00:00:34.260
- I think it would be a lie if y'all did,

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.460
like nobody...you know what I'm saying?

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:37.649
Like, especially with
that many like bold women.

00:00:37.649 --> 00:00:38.482
- Personality.

00:00:38.482 --> 00:00:39.315
- Like, it's like yeah personalities.

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:41.190
it's like if you're an
entertainer in general, like

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.621
that many artists in one place, like

00:00:42.621 --> 00:00:44.306
nobody's gonna agree on everything.

00:00:44.306 --> 00:00:45.139
- Yeah.

00:00:45.139 --> 00:00:47.760
- But I love the fact that
you prove that it can happen.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.650
Like even though we don't
have to always agree on stuff

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:51.210
but it can still come to fruition.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.062
- I mean, I think that's the

00:00:52.062 --> 00:00:54.630
the strength of being in a group, period.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.850
It's like a lot of times
we don't necessarily agree,

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.280
but we want our fans to be happy.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.180
So at the end of the day

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.823
we gonna figure it out
to get on that stage

00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:05.100
and pull that show together
so that our fans can be happy.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.240
Because we love our fans,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.391
we love the support they give us.

00:01:07.391 --> 00:01:09.132
Even if we go crazy backstage.

00:01:09.132 --> 00:01:09.965
- Yeah.

00:01:09.965 --> 00:01:11.820
- We gonna do what we gotta
do to make that show right.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.760
- Yeah. It's more than us, you know

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.593
- [Kandi] Yeah.

00:01:14.593 --> 00:01:15.426
it's more than the performer.

00:01:15.426 --> 00:01:16.650
It's about them. I agree. I agree.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:19.350
Well, Tiny, the idea to perform together

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.790
came from doing verses, right?

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:21.720
- Yes. Yes.

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.010
- This was during Covid.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:23.843
- Yes.

00:01:23.843 --> 00:01:24.676
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:24.676 --> 00:01:28.531
- We had one of the dopest
verses ever, I feel.

00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:30.986
(crowd cheering)

00:01:30.986 --> 00:01:32.070
You know it's a platform where

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:33.870
two different artists or writers

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.850
and they come together, producers

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.350
and they play hit for hit.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.840
You know, they just do, it's
like a little friendly battle,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.030
but that's what started the whole idea

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.730
of us maybe like joining and doing more,

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.010
you know on the road or a show.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.600
- So, LaTocha, you've said that you

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.040
you were not excited about this tour.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.150
Why is that?

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.860
- Well, in the beginning it was that

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:55.080
we had like kinks to iron out, right?

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.766
And so when you go through
those types of things

00:01:56.766 --> 00:01:58.800
you never wanna bring somebody else in.

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.570
It's like having a family dinner, right?

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:01.710
And you're, everybody's having fun

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.030
and all a sudden we get at odds

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:04.500
and then you invite someone else over

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.240
and it's like they're,
that's unfair to them.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.490
- Oh, I've been to
those awkward...No, yeah

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.507
- And that's just not what it is.

00:02:09.507 --> 00:02:10.800
And you talked about Survivor.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.152
This was our survivor.

00:02:12.152 --> 00:02:12.985
(group laughing)

00:02:12.985 --> 00:02:13.860
- [Kelly] Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:14.910
- Without the bugs.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:15.743
- Yeah.

00:02:15.743 --> 00:02:16.576
- Is that hard?

00:02:16.576 --> 00:02:18.060
Like being family and having to

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.700
like talk about stuff like that on air?

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.777
- Uh...

00:02:21.777 --> 00:02:24.000
(group laughing)

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.990
It's a lot, you know, I mean

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.370
but this is our truth,
you know what I mean?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.270
So we go through things

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.560
and I think that this is shed light

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.885
on other families that are looking,

00:02:29.885 --> 00:02:32.280
siblings that are saying,
oh, they got through that

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.260
or This is how they work this out.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.340
Survivor.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.214
- I love Survivor.

00:02:36.214 --> 00:02:37.740
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.640
- That's a lot of families.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:39.838
- Yes.

00:02:39.838 --> 00:02:41.280
- So Tamika as sisters, you and LaTocha

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.050
don't always get along,
as we were just saying.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.660
So do you feel like it's
hard for you personally to,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.700
because I know that me and
my sister are very different.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.996
Like she's more private than I am.

00:02:49.996 --> 00:02:52.290
I am like, what you wanna know?

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.123
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:02:53.123 --> 00:02:53.956
(Tamika laughing)

00:02:53.956 --> 00:02:55.350
- And I probably should
shut my mouth sometimes.

00:02:55.350 --> 00:02:57.360
Like, but like, I'm like
one of those people.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.040
I'm just a total extrovert.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.300
Right. So is it,

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.133
is it hard for you to like

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.120
- Sometimes, Sometimes it's hard just,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.260
not just me and my sister,

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:05.850
but all of us like sisters.

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:06.683
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:08.580
- But it, you know, the
misconception is we're arguing,

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.020
but we just talk loud when we talk.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:10.853
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:10.853 --> 00:03:11.686
- So don't mean we have an argument,

00:03:11.686 --> 00:03:12.780
we're having a loud conversation.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:15.480
- Yeah and even if you
do argue, that's okay.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.620
Like I feel like if you don't

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:18.090
then you're never gonna have progress

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.820
and you're never gonna
own your real truth.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.653
(laughter)

00:03:20.653 --> 00:03:21.990
Yeah. You have to argue.

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:22.823
- We definitely argue.

00:03:22.823 --> 00:03:23.656
- That's normal.

00:03:23.656 --> 00:03:24.489
- This one here

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.490
- I'm the plus box

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:27.913
- This the queen of arguing.

00:03:27.913 --> 00:03:28.920
(group laughing)

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.390
- I love it, could have been a lawyer.

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.450
So Lelee this year is the
30th anniversary of SWV,

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.879
so how have y'all managed
to get, that's amazing!

00:03:35.879 --> 00:03:37.350
(crowd applauding)

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.463
How have you managed to stay together?

00:03:39.463 --> 00:03:40.590
Like that's, you know what I'm saying?

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.597
Just pulling together
constantly that, look at

00:03:42.597 --> 00:03:44.100
- Oh my God

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:44.933
- Your face.

00:03:44.933 --> 00:03:46.818
- Sometimes we don't.

00:03:46.818 --> 00:03:47.651
- Yeah.

00:03:47.651 --> 00:03:49.530
- You know, but you know, it the, we have

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.252
such amazing fans and sometime the journey

00:03:52.252 --> 00:03:54.480
is more important than the problem.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:55.313
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:55.313 --> 00:03:56.146
- And I think that's what

00:03:56.146 --> 00:03:56.979
- [Kelly] Wow, well said

00:03:56.979 --> 00:03:58.920
- that's why we're here
today as well as Xscape.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.060
You know, we love each other,

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.743
but sometimes what sister you know,

00:04:01.743 --> 00:04:03.210
that you don't have a fight with

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.470
you don't have a problem with.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:06.180
It's normal, you know?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.420
But we are stronger
together than we are part.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:10.253
- Amen.

00:04:10.253 --> 00:04:11.730
- And we've grown so much.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.961
We've grown over the years.

00:04:12.961 --> 00:04:13.921
(crowd applauding)

00:04:13.921 --> 00:04:14.997
- And we grew up in this industry.

00:04:14.997 --> 00:04:16.654
We were young, we were teenagers.

00:04:16.654 --> 00:04:17.487
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:17.487 --> 00:04:19.410
- So our journey, we were learning lessons

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.910
as we went along

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:22.560
and sometimes we just

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:24.570
we're getting it right in the public.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.403
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:25.403 --> 00:04:26.340
- You know, we're growing in the public,

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.690
so that's what you guys see.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.171
- We, we've learned to
respect one another.

00:04:29.171 --> 00:04:30.060
- Yeah.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.920
- Cause we didn't always
respect one another

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:35.358
- Everybody give it up for
the women of SWV and Xscape

00:04:35.358 --> 00:04:37.465
- (crowd cheering)

